From 848a4cadce8dcc5e931bc576babffbef5ccdac61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EmberGate <embergate@local>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:36:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] qwen35 HC: optional per-pass read gates
 (<arch>.residual_gate_map + pass.k.hc_*) (EmberGate T-052)

A uint32 array <arch>.residual_gate_map, one entry per <arch>.layer_schedule position, names the gate set each
position reads: g < n file trunk layers = blk.g.hc_* (what every position reads without the key), g >= n = the extra
set pass.(g - n).hc_{mix,mlp}.{gain,w_a,w_u,w_v} (or gain + w_u + w_av, the fused W-188 form). The sets are created
in the buffer of the file layer whose position reads them first; the schedule expansion points each position's hc_*
at its set, so the graph (build_hc_read / fused ops) is unchanged.

No key: identical behaviour (CPU logit files byte-identical on the seated HC files). Refusals name the position and
tensor: map length != schedule, map without schedule or without residual_streams, a set no position reads, a
missing pass tensor, pass.* tensors without the map. An engine without this patch refuses a file with pass.*
tensors ("wrong number of tensors").
